  "body": "## Dependent #274 AVX2 stage \u2014 draft, no promotion\n\nUses John's three-commit `f84c3e4ea918b4fa4d99e4f09956b4e6cc96f602` rebase on the current #271 candidate, not another implementation. The test conflict preserves both ISA-width reachability and selected-state reset assertions. The distinct-index debug contract and valid-input tests remain.\n\nThe eight-lane kernel/generator/theorem match frozen #274 `e3af185c5962076972129e83dfc2c8d9badb62b2` byte-for-byte; sixteen-lane bytes retain frozen #271 `7c4166fa922165c7db8250908f6442cb3b9a28a2`. Dedicated output8 generation/proof and its cache identity are registered alongside output16. No API type, Hasher field or thread-policy knob is added.\n\nFresh native/reference/proof checks are being prepared. **A physical AVX2 performance gate is pending**: the existing Cherry Zen3 host has no authenticated ED25519 enrollment in this strict client, so no unchecked SSH fallback or substitute native-speed claim is made. Devon owns physical i7 measurements. Original frozen data are prior evidence, not new-source results.\n\nDependencies #295 then #296 remain explicit. The #296 pipeline doctest failure and #270 cost reviews remain holds; a passing new run does not erase that failure or establish an engine fix. This stage is not ready to land. Startup/finish/sparse/control costs will accompany current-source complete-work data; no global Pareto claim or composed ratios.\n\nNo organization merge/release/tag/upload by Sam; no multithreading tuning or new rental.\n\n\u2014 Sam Shackleton\n",
